From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:20:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] lazarus-canary: the canary sidecar (SOV-P-002 W9)

A Python service outside primed, with a systemd unit that is shipped but
not installed. Per round it places, for each due gateway with a registered
node, an own canary C/C' (C deprioritised on the pool node before it
exists, then pushed over one P2P connection to that node only; C' to the
pool node), plus one shared canary (market fee, pre-prioritised under the
pool's -blockmintxfee) and one decoy (zero fee, prioritised on the pool
node only), and reports each to primed (POST /sovereignty/canary with the
token and kind). Cadence per SOV-P-002 section 5 from primed's own report.

The canary key signs only on a signer node through signrawtransactionwithkey;
the RPC clients are allowlisted per role, so the signer can never be asked
to broadcast and the pool node never gets a key or wallet-signing call.
Startup and every scan refuse to run if a pool-node wallet knows the canary
address. Settled pairs return to the UTXO list with their fee booked.
Shared canaries are released after 600 s so the pool can mine them.
SOCKS5 (Tor) delivery is written, framing-tested only.

The in-repo A2 feeders post template checks (demo route) now that canary
evidence comes from checks; rnd-a2-demo.sh takes KNOTS_BASE and RPC_PORT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
