+++ b/lazarus/canary/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# lazarus-canary
+
+Places the Sovereign TIDES canaries that primed judges gateways by (SOV-P-002 W9; the detector is
+W8 in `prime/`). A Python service with no dependencies beyond the standard library (3.11+). It is
+shipped with a systemd unit that is **not installed**: it starts at stage S3 (the canary shadow).
+
+```
+python3 lazarus_canary.py -c lazarus-canary.toml check-isolation   # the pool node's wallets must not know the canary address
+python3 lazarus_canary.py -c lazarus-canary.toml scan              # rebuild the UTXO list (scantxoutset; slow on mainnet)
+python3 lazarus_canary.py -c lazarus-canary.toml once              # one round now
+python3 lazarus_canary.py -c lazarus-canary.toml run               # the service
+python3 lazarus_canary.py -c lazarus-canary.toml status
+python3 -m unittest test_lazarus_canary                            # unit tests, no node needed
+```
+
+## What one round does
+| Kind | Tx | Where it goes | What an honest gateway does |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **own** (per due gateway G) | C and C′ spend the same canary UTXO; C′ pays `twin_extra_sats` more | `prioritisetransaction C 0 -1e8` on the pool node **first**; C over one P2P connection to G's registered node only; C′ to the pool node | templates C (the pool node never can) |
+| **shared** (one per round) | D at the market fee | `prioritisetransaction D` on the pool node to a modified feerate under its `-blockmintxfee`, **then** `sendrawtransaction D` to the pool node | templates D (relayed everywhere on its base fee; the pool node keeps it and never templates it) |
+| **decoy** (one per round) | Q with zero fee | `prioritisetransaction Q +decoy_delta_sats`, then `sendrawtransaction Q 0` to the pool node | never has Q (under every relay floor); the pool node templates it |
+
+Each canary is reported to primed with `POST /sovereignty/canary`
+`{"gateway": G | "*", "t": <delivered>, "txid", "kind"}` and the `X-Sovereignty-Token` header (the
+token file primed writes in its data dir). An own canary makes primed fetch G's newest job about 45 s
+later (`request_full_block`); shared canaries and decoys are read from the same job lists.
+
+Everything pays back to the canary address. After each round the sidecar settles earlier canaries:
+`gettxout` on the pool node tells which of C / C′ (or D, Q) confirmed; that output goes back on the
+UTXO list and the fee is booked in `state_dir/canaries.jsonl` (`"event": "placed"` and
+`"event": "resolved"`, with `which` = `C` or `C'` and `fee`). A canary whose input is still unspent
+after `inflight_max_secs` and that no mempool holds is released. A delivery that fails is never
+reported to primed, its C is re-prioritised back and its UTXO kept.
+
+A shared canary is evidence only while primed can judge it (jobs up to 180 s after it). After
+`fees.shared_release_secs` (600 s) the sidecar lifts its priority on the pool node, so the pool can
+mine it as well; otherwise only other pools' blocks would, and on a chain where Lazarus finds most
+blocks its UTXO would stay locked.
+
+The sidecar also reads each C / D back out of the pool node's `getblocktemplate` after a round and
+logs `LEAK` if one is there (`status.leaks`).
+
+## Cadence (SOV-P-002 §5)
+Per gateway, from primed's `/sovereignty.json` row: new or suspect (fewer than `new_until_due`
+canaries judged) every `new_secs` (1,200 s); flagged every `flagged_secs` (1,200 s); clean (≥
+`clean_min_due` judged, own hit rate ≥ `clean_min_rate`) every `clean_secs` (14,400 s); otherwise
+`enrolled_secs` (3,600 s). Each interval is drawn from base × (1 ± `jitter`) (0.5). A round runs at
+most every `round_min_gap_secs` (1,200 s) and takes every gateway due by then, plus one shared canary
+and one decoy. Gateways come from `[[gateways]]` (G, node) and `nodes_file` (read every round;
+W10's `sovereignty-nodes.json` once it lands). A gateway with `node = "none"` is never canaried.
+
+## Keys and isolation
+- The canary key is a WIF in `wallet.key_file`. The sidecar refuses a key file readable by group or
+  others. Keep the key in Proton Pass and write the file at install (`pass-cli`, see the
+  `proton-pass` skill); it never goes in git or a vault note.
+- It is used in exactly one place: `signrawtransactionwithkey` on the **signer** node, with the
+  prevout given explicitly. The signer should run with `-connect=0 -listen=0 -disablewallet`. The
+  sidecar's RPC client for it allows only `signrawtransactionwithkey`, `getdescriptorinfo`,
+  `deriveaddresses` and `validateaddress`, so it can never ask the signer to broadcast.
+- The pool node's RPC client allows no key or wallet-signing method at all. At start (and on every
+  `scan`) the sidecar asks each of the pool node's wallets about the canary address and refuses to
+  run if any has it as mine, watch-only or solvable (`check-isolation`).
+- The pool node never sees C before it is deprioritised, and never holds a canary key: C′, D and Q
+  reach it as raw transactions.
+
+## Pool-node requirements
+- `-blockprioritysize=0`. Knots' coin-age area otherwise adds the first below-minimum-priority tx
+  whatever its fee delta, and a deprioritised C or D reaches the template (SOV-004).
+- `-blockmintxfee` above its relay floor, set in `pool_node.blockmintxfee_satvb`. A shared canary
+  sits halfway between the two unless `fees.shared_modified_satvb` says otherwise.
+- The getblocktemplate/submitblock RPC stays private: `getrawmempool true` (`fees.modified`) and
+  `getprioritisedtransactions` show which txs are canaries.
+
+## Delivery
+`delivery.mode = "direct"` pushes C over plain TCP from this host (v1 P2P: version/verack, `tx`,
+then `ping` and wait for the `pong`, which the node sends only after it processed the `tx`). A canary
+from the pool's own IP is recognisable, so production should use `mode = "socks5"` with
+`proxy = "127.0.0.1:9050"` (Tor), which also reaches `.onion` nodes. **The SOCKS5 path is written
+and unit-tested for its framing only; it has not been run against Tor** (SOV-008 used direct P2P on
+regtest). Nodes that only speak BIP324 v2 are not supported.
+
+## Files
+| Path | What |
+|---|---|
+| `lazarus_canary.py` | the service and CLI |
+| `xbt_p2p.py` | one-shot P2P delivery (and SOCKS5) |
+| `lazarus-canary.toml.example` | every config key with its default |
+| `lazarus-canary.service` | systemd unit (not installed) |
+| `test_lazarus_canary.py` | unit tests |
+
+Demo: `~/xbt-rnd/sov-008/canary-sidecar-demo.sh` (SOV-008).
